(1329,2857,'Inflammation of the lining of the stomach and intestines, often accompanied by diarrhea.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5228FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1330,2860,'The exposure of root surface by an apical shift in the position of the gingiva.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5188FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1331,2861,'An ocular disease, occurring in many forms, having as its primary characteristics an unstable or a sustained increase in the intraocular pressure which the eye cannot withstand without damage to its structure or impairment of its function. The consequences of the increased pressure may be manifested in a variety of symptoms, depending upon type and severity, such as excavation of the optic disk, hardness of the eyeball, corneal anesthesia, reduced visual acuity, seeing of colored halos around lights, disturbed dark adaptation, visual field defects, and headaches. (Dictionary of Visual Science, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1332,2862,'Swelling of the thyroid gland, mainly due to iodine deficiency','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'16215FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1333,2863,'Acute infectious disease characterized by primary invasion of the urogenital tract. The etiologic agent, NEISSERIA GONORRHOEAE, was isolated by Neisser in 1879.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5176FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1334,2864,'Hereditary metabolic disorder characterized by recurrent acute arthritis, hyperuricemia and deposition of sodium urate in and around the joints, sometimes with formation of uric acid calculi.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5171FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1335,2865,'Disruption of structural continuity of the body as a result of the discharge of firearms.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5162FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1336,2866,'Lateral displacement of the great toe, producing deformity of the first metatarsophalangeal joint with callous, bursa, or bunion formation over the bony prominence.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5149FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1337,2867,'An extremely common benign tumor, occurring most commonly in infancy and childhood, made up of newly formed blood vessels, and resulting from malformation of angioblastic tissue of fetal life. It can occur anywhere in the body but is most frequently noticed in the skin and subcutaneous tissues. About 75% are present at birth, and about 60% occur in the head and neck area. The majority in infancy will regress spontaneously. Some hemangiomas grow rapidly during the early months of life and may be a source of some concern, although virtually all disappear by about 5 years of age. They do not metastasize and simple excision will often be curative. (Dorland, 27th ed; from Stedman, 25th ed; DeVita Jr et al., Cancer: Principles &amp;amp; Practice of Oncology, 3d ed, p1355)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5137FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1338,2868,'Bleeding into the joints. It may arise from trauma or spontaneously in patients with hemophilia.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5135FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1339,2869,'Frank bleeding in the gastrointestinal tract.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5132FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1340,2870,'Severe or complete loss of motor function on one side of the body. This condition is usually caused by BRAIN DISEASES that are localized to the cerebral hemisphere opposite to the side of weakness. Less frequently, BRAIN STEM lesions; cervical SPINAL CORD DISEASES; PERIPHERAL NERVOUS SYSTEM DISEASES; and other conditions may manifest as hemiplegia. The term hemiparesis (see PARESIS) refers to mild to moderate weakness involving one side of the body.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5125FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1341,2871,'A group of inherited disorders characterized by structural alterations within the hemoglobin molecule.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5114FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1342,2872,'A form of anemia in which the bone marrow fails to produce adequate numbers of peripheral blood elements.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5110FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1343,2875,'A self-limited hemorrhagic disorder of the first days of life, caused by a deficiency of the vitamin K-dependent blood coagulation factors II, VII, IX, and X. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5104FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1344,2876,'Severe inability of the liver to function normally, as evidenced by severe jaundice and abnormal levels of ammonia, bilirubin, alkaline phosphatase, glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase, lactic dehydrogenase, and reversal of the albumin/globulin ratio. (Blakiston&amp;amp;#39;s Gould Medical Dictionary, 4th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5099FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1345,2877,'Protrusion of a loop or knuckle of an organ or tissue through an abnormal opening.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5079FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1346,2878,'Abnormal protrusion of the intestine through the abdominal muscles.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5077FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1347,2879,'A personality disorder characterized by overly reactive and intensely expressed or overly dramatic behavior, proneness to exaggeration, emotional excitability, and disturbances in interpersonal relationships.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5059FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1348,2880,'A malignant disease characterized by progressive enlargement of the lymph nodes, spleen, and general lymphoid tissue, and the presence of large, usually multinucleate, cells (REED-STERNBERG CELLS) of unknown origin.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5058FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1349,2881,'A circumscribed collection of fluid, especially a collection of fluid in the tunica vaginalis of the testicle or along the spermatic cord. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5047FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1350,2882,'A behavior disorder originating in childhood in which the essential features are signs of developmentally inappropriate inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity. Although most individuals have symptoms of both inattention and hyperactivity-impulsivity, one or the other pattern may be predominant. The disorder is more frequent in males than females. Onset is in childhood. Symptoms often attenuate during late adolescence although a minority experience the full complement of symptoms into mid-adulthood. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5044FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1351,2884,'Disorders characterized by hypersomnolence during normal waking hours that may impair cognitive functioning. Subtypes include primary hypersomnia disorders (e.g., IDIOPATHIC HYPERSOMNOLENCE; NARCOLEPSY; and KLEINE-LEVIN SYNDROME) and secondary hypersomnia disorders where excessive somnolence can be attributed to a known cause (e.g., drug affect, MENTAL DISORDERS, and SLEEP APNEA SYNDROME). (From  J Neurol Sci 1998 Jan 8;153(2):192-202; Thorpy, Principles and Practice of Sleep Medicine, 2nd ed, p320)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5014FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1352,2885,'Persistently high arterial blood pressure. Currently accepted threshold levels are 140 mm Hg systolic and 90 mm Hg diastolic pressure.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:15',NULL,NULL,'5012FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1353,2886,'Hypertrophy or enlargement of the heart.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:16',NULL,NULL,'5005FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1354,2887,'The condition that results from excessive loss of body water.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:16',NULL,NULL,'4978FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1355,2888,'Thrombocytopenia occurring in the absence of toxic exposure or a disease associated with decreased platelets. It is mediated by immune mechanisms, in most cases IgG autoantibodies which attach to platelets and subsequently undergo destruction by macrophages. The disease is seen in acute (affecting children) and chronic (adult) forms.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:02:16',NULL,NULL,'4968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
